{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"tail -30 rehearsal/README.md && cat rehearsal/files.mjs && sed -n '1,68p' rehearsal/test/runner.test.mjs\"","aggregated_output":"- Keep passes, failures and timeouts as counted outcomes. Only voids and infrastructure failures leave slots open. A CLI authentication or provider failure or an exit before a model turn is an infrastructure failure. The runner records the reason and uses saved transcripts to identify older infrastructure failures. Rerun the same batch to fill open slots after inspecting the saved reason. The new record links to the record it replaces. A harness timeout still counts if there is no evidence of a CLI infrastructure failure, even if killing the process truncates the transcript and leaves the audit unverifiable.\n- The owner decided on 2026-11-19 that the 1.0 rehearsal rule requires at least two passes in three counted slots in each of the eight agent × task cells. The summary shows the counts and rule status for each cell, the batch totals, and the recorded failures. It also checks that counted records use matching docs, package, task inputs, grader, tool versions and observed model IDs. Keep the release candidate and CLI installations fixed while collecting a batch. An empty summary displays zero counts for all cells.\n- Report this as “agent rehearsal: these prompts, these models, Chrome; not user evidence”. With three independent runs per cell, the two-sided exact 95% binomial interval is 9.43% to 99.16% for two successes and 29.24% to 100% for three. The counts apply to these line and bar tasks in Chrome and do not establish general success rates or human usability.\n\n## Isolation and audit\n\nEach attempt gets a newly created directory outside the repository with a fresh home, temporary storage and workspace. The workspace contains copies of the published docs, the unpacked package, primary data and prompt, and a writable location for `chart.js` and its helpers. The docs retain published examples and exclude internal source snapshots. The runner applies `chmod -R a-w` to `docs/` and `node_modules/` and removes write permission from the fixture, prompt and package manifest. These file modes protect against accidental writes. A sufficiently privileged or same-owner subprocess can still change modes or replace inputs. The runner verifies staged input hashes before grading, and the browser grader supplies canonical data from the harness.\n\n- **Codex CLI 0.170.0.** The runner assigns a fresh `CODEX_HOME` and symlinks only `auth.json` from the real login. It uses `--ignore-user-config` and `--ignore-rules`, disables apps, plugins, memory and hooks, skips host skill discovery, and disables web search. It uses `-s workspace-write`, `-a never`, and `sandbox_workspace_write.network_access=false`. The CLI help describes `--sandbox` as selecting the sandbox for “model-generated shell commands” and says `--ignore-user-config` still uses `CODEX_HOME` for auth. Workspace-write applies write and network restrictions to agent commands. It allows host reads, and Codex's shell can run more than Node. The prompt and audit constrain use of that wider surface.\n- **Claude Code 2.1.327.** Each attempt has a fresh `HOME` and `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. With an API key, the runner passes it through and uses `--bare`, which skips OAuth, auto-memory and `CLAUDE.md` discovery. For OAuth the only initial config entry is a `.credentials.json` symlink into the real home. The runner creates and removes the symlink without opening the credential file. The fresh config and staged workspace contain no local Claude customizations or saved memory. Without `--bare`, `--safe-mode` disables `CLAUDE.md` discovery, skills, installed plugins, hooks and other customizations, and `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1` turns off auto-memory. Built-in plugins, admin-managed settings and managed plugin hooks can still apply.\n- Both Claude modes keep `--restricted`, which ignores user, project and local settings and confines file tools to working directories. `--strict-mcp-config` limits MCP to the supplied empty configuration, `--disable-slash-commands` disables skills and commands, and `--no-session-persistence` turns off session saves in print mode. The built-in allowlist exposes file tools and Bash, with `--allowedTools` limiting Bash permission to `node …` and `dontAsk` denying other calls. `--permission-prompts none` denies anything that would prompt. Web tools and Chrome are absent. A Node subprocess can have host filesystem and network access through the operating system.\n- Both CLIs need their provider transport. These CLI controls give fresh session state and restrict configured tools. They do not provide a filesystem namespace or a transport-only network policy for Claude's Node subprocess. For strictly enforced docs-only reads and network isolation, use external isolation that enforces those boundaries for both CLIs. Keep host managed policies fixed and record them with the rehearsal if they apply.\n\nThe audit requires a parseable transcript with the CLI's start and terminal events. Empty, malformed, or truncated transcripts are **unverifiable**. Recorded out-of-workspace paths and excluded tool calls are a second check. Detection covers recorded tool inputs, literal command paths, and symlink targets that can be resolved when auditing. It cannot observe a subprocess's actual reads, dynamically constructed paths or fetches from Node code. “No findings” describes the transcript only.\n\nEach record stores `run.json` with the CLI version, arguments, requested and observed model metadata, elapsed time and status, and SHA-256 hashes of both inputs, their expected results, the prompt, copied docs, packed library and grader. Claude records include `claudeMode` as `bare` or `fresh-config`. The record also stores the transcript, stderr, answer files if present, and the grade and Chrome version if the answer reached Chrome. The disposable workspace and home, including the credential symlink, are removed after saving the record. An interrupted batch may leave an incomplete record or scratch directory.\n\n## Reader grading and verification\n\nThe grader uses clean headless Chrome contexts in Los Angeles and Tokyo with English (US) as the page locale. Each answer must handle the original and changed-value input. The alternate signups input has an absent value field that should produce an omission note. Dates are graded as calendar days, including unambiguous month-first and day-first forms. Series labels must match the requested fields. The fixtures declare no measurement unit or currency. The grader opens the standard table control, checks caption, semantic headers and rows, reads the plotted x order and SVG stroke breaks, samples the first calendar date through the plot control, and checks title clipping and omission counts in both the visible note and the accessibility tree.\n\nTo regrade, use a workspace with the same packed package installed and the saved answer files restored into it.\n\n```sh\nnode rehearsal/grade.mjs --task daily-visits --workdir /path/to/prepared/workspace\nnpx --no-install vitest run --root rehearsal --exclude '**/*.browser.test.mjs'\nnpx --no-install vitest run --root rehearsal\n```\n\nThe first Vitest command runs fixture, comparator, audit and local-runner tests without Chrome. The second also runs the browser references and negative controls. The runner exits 0 when all newly scheduled attempts pass or there are no open slots, 1 for any new failed, timed-out or void attempt, and 2 for setup or infrastructure errors. Use the summary to evaluate the whole release rehearsal.\nimport { readFile, rename, rm, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { isAbsolute, join, relative, sep } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath, pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\n\nexport const rehearsal = fileURLToPath(new URL('.', import.meta.url));\nexport const repository = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url));\nexport const tasks = ['daily-visits', 'regional-sales', 'signups', 'daily-revenue'];\n\nexport function inside(root, file) {\n  const path = relative(root, file);\n  return path !== '..' && !path.startsWith('..' + sep) && !isAbsolute(path);\n}\n\nexport function taskFiles(task) {\n  if (!task || !/^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/.test(task)) throw new Error('Supply a task ID from rehearsal/prompts.');\n  return {\n    prompt: join(rehearsal, 'prompts', task + '.md'),\n    fixture: join(rehearsal, 'fixtures', task + '.json'),\n    expected: join(rehearsal, 'fixtures', task + '.expected.json'),\n    alternate: join(rehearsal, 'fixtures', task + '.alternate.json'),\n    alternateExpected: join(rehearsal, 'fixtures', task + '.alternate.expected.json'),\n  };\n}\n\nexport async function readJson(file) {\n  return JSON.parse(await readFile(file, 'utf8'));\n}\n\nexport async function writeJson(file, value) {\n  const temporary = file + '.' + randomUUID() + '.tmp';\n  try {\n    await writeFile(temporary, JSON.stringify(value, null, 2) + '\\n', { flag: 'wx' });\n    await rename(temporary, file);\n  } finally {\n    await rm(temporary, { force: true });\n  }\n}\n\nexport function isMain(url) {\n  return !!process.argv[1] && pathToFileURL(process.argv[1]).href === url;\n}\nimport { access, chmod, copyFile, cp, lstat, mkdir, mkdtemp, open, readFile, readdir, readlink, rm, stat, symlink, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { afterEach, beforeEach, expect, it, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport { agentArgs, agentErrors, agentVersion, observeAgent, runAgent } from '../agent.mjs';\nimport { auditTranscript } from '../audit.mjs';\nimport { readJson, repository } from '../files.mjs';\nimport { grade } from '../grade.mjs';\nimport { cells, effort, models, nextAttempts, protocol, readRecords, summarize, timeoutMs } from '../protocol.mjs';\nimport { attempt, runBatch } from '../run.mjs';\nimport { formatSummary } from '../summary.mjs';\nimport { prepareWorkspace, removeWorkspace } from '../workspace.mjs';\n\nvi.mock('node:fs/promises', async importOriginal => {\n  const fs = await importOriginal();\n  return { ...fs, open: vi.fn(fs.open), readFile: vi.fn(fs.readFile), copyFile: vi.fn(fs.copyFile), cp: vi.fn(fs.cp) };\n});\n\nconst jsonl = (...events) => events.map(event => JSON.stringify(event)).join('\\n');\nconst codexStart = { type: 'thread.started', thread_id: 'thread-id' };\nconst codexLog = (...events) => jsonl(codexStart, { type: 'turn.started' }, ...events, { type: 'turn.completed' });\nconst claudeInit = { type: 'system', subtype: 'init' };\nconst claudeLog = (...events) => jsonl(claudeInit, ...events, { type: 'result', is_error: false });\nconst command = (text, cwd) => ({ type: 'item.completed', item: { type: 'command_execution', command: text, cwd } });\nconst claude = (name, input, model = models.claude) => ({\n  type: 'assistant', message: { model, content: [{ type: 'tool_use', name, input }] },\n});\nconst expiredLogin = 'Failed to authenticate: this login reached its time limit and cannot be renewed. Run `claude auth login` to sign in again…';\nconst expiredLoginLog = jsonl(claudeInit,\n  { type: 'assistant', message: { model: '<synthetic>', content: [{ type: 'text', text: expiredLogin }] } },\n  { type: 'result', subtype: 'success', is_error: true, result: expiredLogin });\n\nlet scratch;\nconst workspaces = [];\nbeforeEach(async () => { scratch = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'axylo-rehearsal-test-')); });\nafterEach(async () => {\n  vi.unstubAllEnvs();\n  for (const directory of workspaces.splice(0)) await removeWorkspace(directory);\n  await rm(scratch, { recursive: true, force: true });\n});\n\nasync function workspaceFor(task, options) {\n  const prepared = await prepareWorkspace(scratch, task, options);\n  workspaces.push(prepared.runDirectory);\n  return prepared;\n}\n\nit('audits complete Codex and Claude logs while allowing the copied docs and system tools', async () => {\n  const codex = codexLog(command(\"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/getting-started.html; node ./chart.js'\", scratch),\n    { type: 'item.completed', item: { type: 'agent_message', text: 'I did not read /home/user/notes.txt.' } });\n  expect(await auditTranscript(codex, scratch, 'codex')).toEqual({\n    status: 'no findings', paths: [], tools: [], malformedLines: 0, problems: [],\n  });\n  const log = claudeLog(claude('Read', { file_path: join(scratch, 'data.json') }));\n  expect(await auditTranscript(log, scratch, 'claude')).toMatchObject({ status: 'no findings' });\n});\n\nit('voids recorded reads of Axylo source, even in otherwise complete transcripts', async () => {\n  const source = join(repository, 'packages/axylo/src/index.ts');\n  expect(await auditTranscript(codexLog(command(`/bin/bash -lc 'cat \"${source}\"'`, scratch)), scratch, 'codex'))\n    .toMatchObject({ status: 'outside policy', paths: [source] });\n  expect(await auditTranscript(claudeLog(claude('Read', { file_path: source })), scratch, 'claude'))\n    .toMatchObject({ status: 'outside policy', paths: [source] });\n});\n\nit('follows recorded relative paths and symlinks out of the workspace', async () => {\n  const workspace = join(scratch, 'workspace');\n  const outside = join(scratch, 'other.txt');\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
